"support.faq.title" = "Frequently Asked Questions";
"support.faq.q1" = "Does Super X provide channels or a subscription?";
"support.faq.a1" = "No. Super X is a player only and comes with no channels, playlists or subscriptions. You add the playlist or Xtream account you received from your own provider, and Super X plays it for you.";
"support.faq.q2" = "Where is my data stored?";
"support.faq.a2" = "Everything stays on this device: your playlists, favorites, watch history, downloads and settings are stored locally in the app. Super X has no servers and nothing about your viewing is uploaded or tracked.";
"support.faq.q3" = "A channel or movie won't play. What should I check?";
"support.faq.a3" = "Most playback problems come from the provider side: an expired subscription, the connection limit on your account being reached, or the provider's server being down. Check the Subscriptions page for the expiry date and run Test Connection in Settings to see a plain-language result.";
"support.faq.q4" = "What does the parental PIN protect?";
"support.faq.a4" = "The PIN guards turning off the adult-content filter, deleting all app data, opening Settings when the settings lock is on, and any categories you lock under Locked Categories. A locked category cannot be opened until the PIN is entered. The PIN is stored only in this device's Keychain and is never included in a backup.";
"support.faq.q5" = "How do I move my setup to a new device?";
"support.faq.a5" = "In Settings, use Backup to export your settings, playlists, favorites and watch-later list to a file, then import that file on the new device. For safety, the settings export does not include playlist passwords — you will be asked to re-enter them during import. A separate full backup that includes passwords also exists, and the app warns you plainly before creating it.";
"support.faq.q6" = "Why does my subscription show as expired?";
"support.faq.a6" = "The expiry date and time come from your provider's own panel — the same answer the provider gives when the app signs in. When that moment passes, the provider stops the streams, and Super X shows the subscription as expired and blocks playback. Renewing with your provider updates the date the next time the app verifies the account.";
